Thread stacks on witos (plan step R6): musl's threads default to 128 KiB, on which the JIT-compiled code of an ordinary
program (expression trees, compiled regular expressions) overflows; CoreCLR's threads take the 1.5 MiB Windows and Apple
give them, beside Apple's branch. Alpine's ENSURE_PRIMARY_STACK_SIZE is not taken: it also grows the primary thread's
stack with alloca, and a started program's first stack on WitOS is a fixed mapping.

